# Configuration for deploy/cloudrun/deploy.sh. Copy to a private file, edit, and pass it with
#   bash deploy.sh --env-file my.env
# The file is sourced by bash: KEY=value lines, no spaces around '=', quote values with spaces.
# Values here override variables already set in your shell. Do not put secrets in this file.
# Variables left commented out use the default shown.

# --- Deployment (read by deploy.sh only) ----------------------------------------------------

# Required. The Google Cloud project to deploy into.
PROJECT_ID=

# Cloud Run, Artifact Registry and (by default) Vertex AI location.
# REGION=us-central1

# Cloud Run service name.
# SERVICE=code-modernizer

# Account id (6-30 chars) of the dedicated runtime service account. Its email is
# <SA_NAME>@<PROJECT_ID>.iam.gserviceaccount.com.
# SA_NAME=modernizer-run

# Artifact Registry Docker repository for the image.
# AR_REPO=code-modernizer

# BigQuery dataset created by deploy/bigquery/setup.sh. The service account is granted write
# access on this dataset only (when bq and jq are installed).
# BQ_DATASET=modernizer

# Image tag for this build. Defaults to a UTC timestamp.
# IMAGE_TAG=

# Deploy an already built image and skip 'gcloud builds submit'.
# IMAGE=

# Also write JSONL result files below this directory inside the container. Cloud Run storage is
# ephemeral and per instance, so this is for debugging only.
# JSONL_SINK_DIR=

# If set, this principal gets roles/run.invoker on the service, e.g. user:you@example.com or
# serviceAccount:ci@my-project.iam.gserviceaccount.com. Nobody else can call the service.
# INVOKER_MEMBER=

# --- Set by deploy.sh, listed for reference (do not set) ------------------------------------
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT   = PROJECT_ID
# MODERNIZER_PROVIDER    = vertex
# MODERNIZER_TELEMETRY   = gcp (Cloud Monitoring metrics and Cloud Trace spans)
# MODERNIZER_SINK        = bigquery:<PROJECT_ID>.<BQ_DATASET>[,jsonl:<JSONL_SINK_DIR>]
# MODERNIZER_RETRIEVAL   = vertex when all three MODERNIZER_VS_* ids below are set, else local
# MODERNIZER_OPEN_BACKEND = endpoint unless you set another value in the open tier section

# --- Vector Search retrieval (optional; leave all three empty to use the local index) -------
# Printed by deploy/vector_search/provision.sh. Set all three or none. Billable, see the README.
# MODERNIZER_VS_INDEX=
# MODERNIZER_VS_ENDPOINT=
# MODERNIZER_VS_DEPLOYED_ID=
# Location of the index and endpoint; defaults to REGION.
# MODERNIZER_VS_LOCATION=
# Embedding model and dimension; the dimension must match the index.
# MODERNIZER_EMBED_MODEL=text-embedding-005
# MODERNIZER_EMBED_DIM=768

# --- Models and routing (forwarded to the service when set) ---------------------------------
# Model ids and locations change over time: check them against the Vertex AI model catalogue.
# MODERNIZER_FRONTIER_MODEL=gemini-2.5-pro
# MODERNIZER_FRONTIER_LOCATION=global
# Default routing policy: always_frontier, always_open or complexity. Requests may override it.
# MODERNIZER_POLICY=complexity
# Difficulty threshold in [0, 1] for the complexity policy. Requests may override it.
# MODERNIZER_THRESHOLD=0.35
# Target share of each request's modules that go to the open model (complexity policy). The
# threshold is then calibrated per request on that batch and takes precedence over
# MODERNIZER_THRESHOLD. A number from 0 to 1; unset means no target. Requests may override it.
# MODERNIZER_OPEN_FRACTION=0.7

# --- Open tier: Gemma 3 12B (REQUIRED unless you choose another backend) ---------------------
# How the open model is reached:
#   endpoint  a Vertex AI endpoint you deployed from Model Garden (the default). Needs
#             MODERNIZER_OPEN_ENDPOINT_ID and MODERNIZER_OPEN_LOCATION; deploy.sh stops with an
#             error if either is missing. See deploy/vertex_gemma/README.md.
#   maas      a Model Garden managed (pay per token) API; the model must be offered in the
#             location below under the id in MODERNIZER_OPEN_MODEL.
#   openai    any OpenAI-compatible server (vLLM, Ollama, GKE ...); needs MODERNIZER_OPEN_BASE_URL.
# A non-empty MODERNIZER_OPEN_BASE_URL takes precedence over the backend setting.
# MODERNIZER_OPEN_BACKEND=endpoint
# Endpoint id only (digits as shown by 'gcloud ai endpoints list'), not the resource path.
# MODERNIZER_OPEN_ENDPOINT_ID=
# Region of the Vertex AI endpoint. It must be the region the endpoint was deployed in.
# MODERNIZER_OPEN_LOCATION=
# Base URL of an OpenAI-compatible server, e.g. https://host/v1 ('/chat/completions' is added).
# MODERNIZER_OPEN_BASE_URL=
# Gemma chat templates have no system role: true puts the system prompt into the user message.
# MODERNIZER_OPEN_FOLD_SYSTEM=true
# Model name sent with each request and used for the price lookup.
# MODERNIZER_OPEN_MODEL=gemma-3-12b-it

# --- Pricing (cost figures in responses and reports) ------------------------------------------
# The packaged price table holds illustrative placeholders, not prices. A self-hosted Gemma
# endpoint is billed per node hour while it is deployed, even when idle, so its per-token rate
# is an amortised figure YOU compute from the node-hour price and a measured throughput
# (deploy/vertex_gemma/README.md). Put it in a YAML file shaped like
# src/modernizer/llm/pricing.yaml. Absolute path INSIDE the container. A file that is not part
# of the image can be mounted from Secret Manager: create a secret from the YAML file and name it
# in PRICING_SECRET; deploy.sh then mounts it at MODERNIZER_PRICING_FILE (default
# /etc/modernizer/pricing.yaml) and lets the service account read it.
# MODERNIZER_PRICING_FILE=/etc/modernizer/pricing.yaml
# PRICING_SECRET=

# --- Pipeline (forwarded when set) -----------------------------------------------------------
# Repair rounds per model tier after the first conversion.
# MODERNIZER_MAX_REPAIRS=2
# Modules converted concurrently inside one request.
# MODERNIZER_WORKERS=4
# Wall-clock limit in seconds for one pytest run of a generated test suite.
# MODERNIZER_TEST_TIMEOUT_S=60

# --- Request limits (forwarded when set) -----------------------------------------------------
# MODERNIZER_MAX_FILES=25
# MODERNIZER_MAX_FILE_CHARS=150000
# MODERNIZER_MAX_TOTAL_CHARS=400000
# In-flight /v1/modernize requests per instance; more get 429 with a Retry-After header.
# MODERNIZER_MAX_CONCURRENT=2
# Seconds advertised in the Retry-After header of a 429.
# MODERNIZER_RETRY_AFTER_S=5
# Python log level of the service.
# MODERNIZER_LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# --- Local and development only --------------------------------------------------------------
# Shared secret for /v1/*: callers send 'Authorization: Bearer <key>'. NOT forwarded by
# deploy.sh. On Cloud Run use IAM instead; Cloud Run IAM reads the same Authorization header.
# MODERNIZER_API_KEY=
